Z||000009||dogtired||12-20-1999||03:39 PM||||About 2 -3  months ago you could still buy them from the publisher. They were $10.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Last time I spoke with them (the publisher), I was told by the sales clerk that one person had purchased all they had left, over 200 and they would no longer be handling them?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>They wouldn't tell me who that person was? Must be that right to privacy thing.<BR>Anyway I figured they would be showing up on one of the lists before long? But haven't seen them yet? OH well just thought you all would like to know what I know?<BR>Not sure they are worth $50, but might be depending on how mechanical one is?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Do not misunderstand the 22P is not a repair manual. it is a illustrated parts manual that shows ALL P/N's. Using it makes it easier to understand how parts relate to each other, and what p/n's are used on what years. It is a good resource.<BR>I would think some will be turning up at swapmeets?  L8er    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
