Z||000013||Raydar||12-22-1999||04:15 PM||||Sure don't. Sorry. <BR>Actually, I don't remember seeing a part#, at all. He sent me some info, in response to an e-mail. It included this...<BR> "1984-88 illustrated parts book, body & chassis, P series, 1000 p, $50."<BR>Seems like I just called him up and told him what I wanted. Only took a couple of days. I was surprised.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-22-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||RossT||12-22-1999||06:16 PM||||I just got my 22-p in the mail today from an auction on e-bay.  I think that the seller must have been the guy that bought the last hundred books.  He sells 3 at a time, all new in shrink rap. As soon as one auction ends, he re-lists it again. I paid $50.00 including shipping.<P>Raydar: I checked out that site, and e-mailed them.  They sent me a list of everything they had for 88 pontiac.They said that the 22-p and shop manuals might be used condition. But the price on th 88 shop manual was great at $60.  They go for $80-$120 on ebay.  If the condition is not bad, I would think that this is a great bargain.<P>That was won of the best links I have seen. Tons of Pontiac print stuff all in one place.<P>Thanks Raydar.  Ross||||reg||1
Z||000015||william_thorniii||12-22-1999||07:40 PM||||Talk about a profit... investment price of approximately 200 manual at $10 assuming no bulk discounts is $2000.  Selling those manuals at an average of $50 makes this clown $8000... that is right $10000.  He probably is a Fiero owner and if he is I would say that we are paying for a new V-8 conversion, body kit, wheels&tires, etc.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||4
